a.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Career Outlook<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>The growing adoption of predictive security is increasing demand for professionals such as AI-based security analysts, SOC engineers, and threat intelligence specialists who can manage and optimize these advanced systems.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">12. AI Security Platforms<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>AI security platforms are specialized systems designed to protect artificial intelligence models, data, and infrastructure from attacks and misuse. As AI adoption grows in 2026, securing models against threats like data poisoning, model theft, and adversarial attacks is becoming a top priority.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why It Matters<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>The global AI security platforms market is expanding quickly, with research projecting growth <a href=\"https:\/\/www.futuremarketinsights.com\/reports\/ai-security-platforms-market?utm_source=chatgpt.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">from around USD 3.5 billion in 2025 to about USD 25.6 billion by 2035<\/a>. This rise reflects the increasing need for advanced tools that can identify vulnerabilities, detect threats in real time, and protect AI systems throughout their lifecycle.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Business Impact<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Organizations use AI security platforms to monitor model behavior, detect vulnerabilities, and prevent unauthorized access. This helps protect sensitive data, maintain compliance, and ensure AI systems operate safely.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Career Outlook<\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Demand is increasing for professionals skilled in AI risk management, model security testing, and adversarial defense as businesses invest in securing their AI ecosystems.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">13. Digital Provenance and Content Authenticity<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Digital provenance and content authenticity technologies help verify the origin and integrit